        "source_sha256": "a3d2e3dc746c357f7c1e0cd399802670ce38f66fb18ef791f381f3866434e926",
        "text": "Deborah Lewis-Virges\n- Home\n- C.H.A.M.P.I.O.N\n- Donate\n- Join Us!\n- Home\n- C.H.A.M.P.I.O.N\n- Donate\n- Join Us!\nSearch by typing & pressing enter\n## YOUR CART\n## Vote Lewis-Virges\nFor East Palo Alto City Council 2026\n|\n## Welcome to the official campaign website for Deborah Lewis-Virges, your candidate for East Palo Alto City Council 2026!​\n|\nMeet the Candidate!\n|\nJoin the Campaign!\n|\nDonate Today!\n|\nDeborah Lewis-Virges is a dedicated community leader with deep roots in East Palo Alto. Her service includes leadership on the Public Works and Transportation Commission, Community Safety Team, and Community Climate Change Team. She also brings more than 20 years of marketing and management experience with Fortune 100 companies and serves as Pastor of Saint Mark AME Zion Church.\nDeborah is running for City Council to champion affordable housing, environmental justice, responsible development, stronger local businesses, and a better quality of life for every resident. Join Deborah in building a stronger and more equitable future for East Palo Alto.\n## SUPPORT KITS AVAILBLE!\n|\n|\nShow your support for the campaign to Move EPA Forward by getting your hands on our exclusive Supporter Kits! Each kit includes:\n- Yard Sign\n- Door Hangers\n- Backpack\n- Custom Campaign Pen\nMessage us (650) 334-8451 to get your kit and help share the vision for moving EPA forward!\n## Endorsements\n​Discover the community leaders, organizations, and residents who are rallying behind Deborah Lewis-Virges for East Palo Alto City Council 2026. This section features a growing list of supporters who share Deborah’s vision for a stronger, more inclusive community. From local advocates to city officials, each endorsement is a testament to Deborah’s commitment to progress and her ability to bring about real change. Hear from those who believe in her leadership and join them in supporting a candidate who will prioritize the well-being of every resident in East Palo Alto.\n|\n​Individuals\nRegina Wallace-Jones, Former EPA Mayor/Councilperson, CFO of ActBlue\nRobert Silano, Director Menlo Park Fire Protection District\nRobert Jones, rEPAt\nRev. Paul Bains, Pastor and Founder of WeHope/Dignitiy on Wheels\nDonna Rutherford, Former EPA Mayor/Councilperson\n|\nAlicia Garcia, COO, WeHope Organization\nRev. Albert Macklin, New Sweet Home Church\nRev. Kelvin Smith, New Community Church\nSharifia Wilson, Former Mayor EPA. Community Archives\nTiffany Hautu, Anamatongi Polyenisian Voices\nViolet Senea, Director CRC\nDerek and Renee Chantler, Chantler & Chantler Law Firm\n## The Candidate with a Clear VIEW!\nPowered by Create your own unique website with customizable templates. Get Started",
        "text_limited": false,
